<title>DUBAI: Saudis pray for rain in response to king's appeal.</title>
<headline>Saudis pray for rain in response to king's appeal.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudis prayed for rainfall across the water-parched kingdom on Monday in response to an appeal by King Fahd last week, Saudi state-run television reported.</p>
<p>Prince Majed, the governor of Mecca, Islam's holiest shrine, led thousands of men in prayers at the Grand Mosque.</p>
<p>Winter rains in Saudi Arabia normally fall at the end of October.</p>
</text>
